[1m[38;5;231mWhich data model and API shape should the preferences store use?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mSingle versioned blob (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mOne localStorage key holding versioned JSON. Atomic writes, central defaults table, migration path. Narrow [39m
     [38;5;246mget/set/reset API.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Key per preference
     [38;5;246mOne localStorage key per setting. Per-key isolation across tabs, but scattered defaults and awkward versioning.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Observable store
     [38;5;246mAdds subscriptions and cross-tab storage events now. Correct for a settings UI, heavy for one preference.[39m
